n `ard` binary for each of darwin/linux x arm64/amd64 (read `dist/artifacts.json`) and `checksums.txt`; run the host-matching binary with `version` and require the output to equal `ard <tag>` where tag is `.tag` in `dist/metadata.json` (what `{{.Tag}}` expanded to); assert the generated cask under `dist/homebrew/Casks/ard.rb` contains no `:no_check` and every URL starts with `https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/releases/`; run `brew audit --cask` on it only when `brew` exists, otherwise print a skip notice.\n3. `Makefile`: add `release-check` to `.PHONY` and a target with a comment (needs goreleaser, not part of `make test`) that runs `deploy/test-release.sh`.\n4. `docs/layout.md`: add `.goreleaser.yaml` and `deploy/test-release.sh` lines to the layout block, mention `make release-check`.\n\n### Test plan\n- `make test` still passes (worker test command); `make lint`.\n- `make release-check` with goreleaser installed: builds all four targets; the version assertion passes; the cask has per-arch sha256.\n- Failure cases: goreleaser absent gives a non-zero exit and an install hint; a missing target in `dist/artifacts.json` fails; a mismatched `ard version` fails.\n- `grep -iE 'token|secret' .goreleaser.yaml` shows only the `{{ .Env.* }}` reference.\n- `brew audit --cask`: a cask with a local path may need `brew audit --cask --new` or a tap context; if it cannot run cleanly in CI, document that in the script header and the PR. Goreleaser and brew are not installed in the worker sandbox (goreleaser is absent here), so the worker should state which checks it could not run.\n\n### Risk\nLow. No Go code, no `.github/` or protected paths change. `.goreleaser.yaml` governs released artifacts but is not in merge.protected_paths; a maintainer may want to protect it. The postflight quarantine removal is an owner-accepted risk. The `{{.Tag}}` snapshot value depends on the nearest tag, hence the metadata-based assertion.\n\n### Size\nM (about 120 changed lines). Files: `.goreleaser.yaml` (new), `deploy/test-release.sh` (new), `Makefile`, `docs/layout.md`.\nEOF\ncat > .ard/306/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a GoReleaser v2 config with the Homebrew cask, a `deploy/test-release.sh` script behind a new `make release-check` target, and layout doc entries. Size M, risk low: no Go code or protected paths change.\n\n## Open issues\n- goreleaser is not installed in the planning environment, so the key names in the cask block must be checked against the pinned GoReleaser version, and `make release-check` and `brew audit --cask` may not be runnable by the worker.\n- The tap token env var name is a placeholder that the later release workflow must supply.\n- A maintainer may want to add `.goreleaser.yaml` to merge.protected_paths.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":856,"cache_read_input_tokens":16416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":856},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7620bae0-cc97-4059-b7aa-ac7fc00b9dd3","uuid":"0fcdc7ae-2a21-44f0-9dd6-c457162d9a51","timestamp":"2026-11-24T17:26:28.301Z","request_id":"req_011ChN9Lr1Ps3BpMjaizC225"}
